{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-07T20:00:06.216Z","author":"codex-sol","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"cd8291c141348235fdc2d72b","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-07T20:00:06.216Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-10-07T20:00:06.216Z","author":"codex-sol","text":"Built-package acceptance baseline: a scratch tracker initialized with the packaged CLI, one tagged task and npm pm-graph 2026.10.5, served by dist/app.js over authenticated HTTP. The real pm-graph export contained generatedAt, workspace, projectKey, nodes and relationships (5 nodes, 4 edges); GET returned 200 but omitted workspace and projectKey, reported extensionAvailable=false and source=pm-web despite installation. Plan: exact-pin the public pure graph builder, consume certified complete rows with noExtensions=true, preserve export fields and ordering, statically observe the project manifest without importing its code, and test generated real trackers, built HTTP parity, observational snapshots and bounded large-corpus reads. Universal output flags on pm-graph export are rejected by the host; report this gap without filing upstream."}]}],"before_hash":"a914387493549ded8dc84580727498bf744f6b565fec6d9f34404bbedc6996ed","after_hash":"c9be688487b6d9620f71e5bfbc55d331e7f7bec0653d8aa8de68a23f03cae714","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"25cf91b5717d05ce6cdeaeacb64e9dbd6eec2f3688cde66c14013de9d2e65e1e"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-07T20:11:44.067Z","author":"codex-sol","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"cd8291c141348235fdc2d72b","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-07T20:11:44.067Z","author":"codex-sol","text":"Implementation uses exact-pinned pm-graph 2026.10.5 graphFromItems for both installed and built-in reads. Generated comparisons exposed the SDK display-order difference; a second public metadata scan now restores export order using only certified rows and rejects identity mismatches. Built overview and neighbor responses retain all export fields and edge attributes. Static manifest observation never imports project code. SDK reads may refresh reconstructible runtime metadata caches even with noExtensions=true; observational snapshots exclude only those named caches and fixture dependency links, while checking item, history, schema, settings and extension bytes. This SDK limitation and the missing certified source-order option are documented and will be reported, not filed upstream."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-07T20:11:44.067Z"}],"before_hash":"c9be688487b6d9620f71e5bfbc55d331e7f7bec0653d8aa8de68a23f03cae714","after_hash":"cd1bb24eea2b2e1cf1d24b64c93a2063b6f8c6d11e14f346795dfb18f9ffc307","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"4f1c9ce492b8eeeede9746d5b49c20